          "text": "You are reading a scanned CTU Argao SAST instructor evaluation form.\n\nReturn TWO things: the handwritten text fields, and the bubble grid.\n\n--- TEXT FIELDS ---\n1. instructor: full name with credentials, as written.\n2. subject: course code matching CTU prefixes (DDMGT, IT, CSO, HCI, ADBAS, IDA) plus digits.\n3. ay_semester: academic year and semester, e.g. '2021', '1st Sem'.\n4. remarks: the exact remark text. It may be English, Tagalog or Bisaya/Cebuano. Fix only obvious OCR typos using context (e.g. 'Danot' -> \"Don't\"). Do not translate, summarise or rewrite.\n5. date: as written, e.g. '01/20/20'.\n6. student_id: digits only.\nGuess messy handwriting. Leave a field as an empty string ONLY if there is no ink at all.\n\n--- BUBBLE GRID ---\nThe form has exactly 20 rated statements in two sections of 10:\n  Management  -> rows 1-10,  report as m1 through m10\n  Performance -> rows 11-20, report as p1 through p10\n\nEach row is answered by shading ONE bubble in a five-column rating scale. The columns are LETTERED, not numbered:\n  O   Outstanding\n  VS  Very Satisfactory\n  S   Satisfactory\n  F   Fair\n  US  Unsatisfactory\n\nFor every one of the 20 rows return exactly one of: O, VS, S, F, US, blank\n\nRules for the grid, follow exactly:\n- Return 'blank' rather than guessing. A wrong letter is worse than a blank here, because a second system cross-checks these values and a confident wrong answer defeats that check.\n- If two bubbles in one row are shaded, return 'blank'.\n- If a mark is very faint but clearly on one column, return that column's letter.\n- Count rows in printed order from the top of each section. Do not skip a row because it looks empty -- return 'blank' for it and keep the numbering aligned.\n- Never shift the numbering to fill gaps. A blank row 7 means m7 is 'blank', not m7 taking row 8's value.\n- Do not convert the letters to numbers. Return the letters.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON matching the schema."
        },
        {
          "inlineData": {
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
            "data": "{{ $('SAST image from phone').item.json.body.image }}"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
